NAME
       tree - show a directory and everything under it as a tree

SYNOPSIS
       tree [-a] [-d] [-f] [-L LEVEL] [-p] [-u] [-g] [-D] [-i] [DIRECTORY]...

DESCRIPTION
       tree draws the contents of DIRECTORY (the current directory by default)
       with lines that show which file is inside which directory, and ends
       with a count of directories and files. It is in the tree package,
       which is not installed by default.

OPTIONS
       -a     Include hidden files (names starting with a dot).

       -d     Show directories only.

       -f     Print the full path of each entry.

       -L LEVEL
              Go at most LEVEL directories deep.

       -p, -u, -g
              Show each entry's permissions, owner, group.

       -D     Show the modification time.

       -i     Do not draw the tree lines.

EXAMPLES
           tree -L 2 /etc/systemd

SEE ALSO
       ls(1), find(1)
